Z||000000||TRiAD||12-09-2001||08:39 PM||||Daniel (FieroAutoXdb or something similar, sorry) fromt eh forum came over today (1.5 hours each way!) to help me try to get my car on the road...The first thing he helped me with (after letting me drive his car on some twisties!) was that legendary clutch pedal replacement procedure. <P> <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0QQAAAHQWv9QXi*vpttd2ewnEitcDtSh6nKZWtb3P8ZqIog0N3wo9U8Z!IWkyyYKGTrz7uyKjRmkf1SaQWPnyAcTGlIQ!b5hdxdaT39vv*C8/Proper-position-1.jpg"> <P>This procedure requires some strange contortions, and the perfection of speaking in strange tongues.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0QQBpAHUW6tQXi*vpttd2ewnEitcDtSh66s1fGFy34U5P9Els2EwKI6KMII7iUi1O7d9cKbVunVChNfOG5EQlyg607E61Q6xR3cTSEVR8fVo/Proper-position-2.jpg"> <P>All in all, it went fairly well, and we have hopefully tracked down the actual cause for the problem...a cracked master cylinder! (It was electrical-taped up on the underside, where the crack is...)<P>Anyway, though you'd get a kick out of this, and I wanted to say a big +<B><FONT COLOR="blue">T H A N K S !!!!!!!</B></FONT> to Daniel...<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0QwBlO10XBwtwZZqI3Om69ptsim8sbgsv6htbwTK5nTjOTXqfhFmE7PufW3uqtRZBdEgZz0PO6pMaCru!KJ*SRcaq8o*iHyw9Pc8KZEv!vcY/Signature-pic-small.jpg">     <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B> ~ Photoshop rendition of planned modifications</I></FONT>||||reg||6
